defragged_task_instance(im_defrag_02959e3f7378d3f1720167a1_1,
    'IM-G8-U3-L4',
    curriculum_task(section(2)),
    defragged_task{evidence_sha256:"df9ac3bb0a401958b8f4e327c5e66d961d6b324f53adf3c596033e24542c8a7b", status:blocked_missing_visual, blocker:expression_missing_from_markdown, complete_statement:"1. Elena babysits her neighbor's children. Her earnings are given by the equation , where represents the number of hours she worked, and represents the amount of money she earned in dollars. Jada earns $7 per hour mowing her neighbors' lawns. a. Who makes more money after working 12 hours? How much more do they make? Explain your reasoning by creating a graph or a table. b. What is the value of the rate of change for each situation, and what does each value mean? c. Using your graph or table, determine how long it would take each person to earn $150. 2. Clare and Han have summer jobs stuffing envelopes for two different companies. Han earns $15 for every 300 envelopes he finishes. Clare's earnings can be seen in the table. | number of envelopes | money earned in dollars | |-----------------------|---------------------------| | 400 | 40 | | 900 | 90 | a. By creating a graph, show how much money each person makes after stuffing 1,500 envelopes. b. What is the value of the rate of change for each situation, and what does each value mean? c. Using your graph, determine how much more money one person makes relative to the other after stuffing 1,500 envelopes. Explain or show your reasoning. 3. Tyler plans to start a lemonade stand and is trying to perfect his recipe for lemonade. He wants to make sure the recipe doesn't use too much lemonade mix (lemon juice and sugar) but still tastes good. Recipe 1 is given by the equation , where represents the amount of lemonade mix in cups, and represents the amount of water in cups. Recipe 2 is given in the table. | lemonade mix (cups) | water (cups) | |-----------------------|----------------| | 10 | 50 | | 13 | 65 | | 21 | 105 | a. If Tyler had 16 cups of lemonade mix, how many cups of water would he need for each recipe? Explain your reasoning by creating a graph or a table. b. What is the value of the rate of change for each recipe, and what does each value mean? c. Tyler has 16 cups of lemonade mix to use for his lemonade stand. Which lemonade recipe should he use? Explain or show your reasoning.", statement_joiner:" ", statement_segments:[seg_0facbf605e12da155a8e, seg_ec2c23482ea47c215527, seg_4b3d5c5365c3e0da5502, seg_9159f60d2d8fa0f4e4d4, seg_636266f93f995d5567ba, seg_c8d6e63abb5824f2ae1a, seg_a31b30edbe8bdfec3e31, seg_351527167b3c7fbce479, seg_27ed450217e1b60d511b, seg_69b770632346c3fd3a3e, seg_fcf3e7fdbe17c8e1b46b, seg_1ccdfdc7255318a33ff3, seg_d1983feb865f996e79cd, seg_f8ed29132576af7c3be2, seg_1212eb790cec5b26f8cb, seg_2f4c79ffb130a1b0b531, seg_a4e309e3e60ab4bb603c, seg_42b5e9aab781ccb3c486, seg_fc5f8e62ae98cc23453a, seg_d093176fffa5503758db, seg_60aa2ad847c1ea754ae8, seg_5f1de831c4d207cd8db2, seg_41f9c77e4dd1f7bf562f, seg_508f6fbbe854fe872738, seg_8e15543c164c6fdeeb5b, seg_2ae5dfe4cbde57dc7c9d, seg_f7692e28bd944118005e, seg_808a88f4899e11bb7fa6, seg_b7b9e4f7956c9e49aa0f, seg_63ca2f7560d4000a5cd2, seg_d1ddd7f03e9897f943eb, seg_c9b2fcfd2f8c3d484509, seg_d4e27d0cf6bda1ebae58, seg_ac35e8ff3cbd0f2eb6b4, seg_6a44d87eaf8042bcf0f3, seg_b9aa3cfaf15b098dd2f7, seg_d8c665bc9a9dfec7fb64, seg_67aa89857e99fa4d5eee, seg_91b30519f33c65a52d2b, seg_ee1aaab7d3c0faa1b9f0], referents:[referent{surface:"in the table", kind:table, status:missing, segments:[seg_c0f2fb4d98e4af3e1eba], antecedent:"", antecedent_segments:[], absence_reason:antecedent_not_in_available_source}], visuals:[visual{surface:"a graph", status:excluded_docling_asset, asset:"hermes/app/runtime/experiments/gemma4_tutor/docling/full-output/TeacherLessonGuides/Grade8/Grade8-3-4-Lesson-teacher-guide-/document_artifacts", source_segments:[seg_73a9fd4ca413c442355c]}], source_segments:[segment{id:"seg_0facbf605e12da155a8e", path:"hermes/app/runtime/experiments/gemma4_tutor/docling/full-output/TeacherLessonGuides/Grade8/Grade8-3-4-Lesson-teacher-gui