egin{cases} \\ y = 4 . 5 x + 1 5 \\\\ \\ y = 5 x + 1 2 . 5 \\end{cases}$$ $$\\begin{cases} & . \\ \\{ \\ y = 5 x - 4 & . \\ \\{ \\ y = 0 . \\\\ & \\ y = 4 x + 1 2 & . \\\\ & . \\ \\{ \\ y = \\frac { 2 } { 3 } x - 4 & . \\ \\{ \\ y = 4 . \\\\ & . \\ \\{ \\ y = - \\frac { 4 } { 3 } x + 9 & . \\ \\{ \\ y = 5 x \\end{cases}$$ $$\\cdot \\begin{cases} \\ y = \\frac { 2 } { 3 } x - 4 \\\\ \\ y = - \\frac { 4 } { 3 } x + 9 \\end{cases}$$ $$-$$ $$-$$ 1. Without solving, identify 3 systems that you think would be the least difficult for you to solve and 3 systems you think would be the most difficult. Be prepared to explain your reasoning. 2. Choose 4 systems to solve. At least one should be from your \"least difficult\" list and one should be from your \"most difficult\" list."),extraction_status(blocked_layout),blocker(expression_missing_without_visual),visual_provenance([]))}).

